+   **The browser run (slice GG5a, 26 November 2026; `apps/pages/test/csp/map.spec.ts`, Chromium and WebKit).**
+   MapLibre 6.19 draws under this policy unchanged: no `blob:` and no `unsafe-eval` are needed, so map pages
+   take no exception. Its `blob:` image path is taken only in a browser without `createImageBitmap`, and its
+   `eval` only through `setRTLTextPlugin` or `importScriptInWorkers` with a classic script, which no page
+   calls. Three conditions the map pages keep: the worker file is named on the page's own origin (another
+   origin makes MapLibre use a `blob:` worker, which `worker-src 'self'` refuses); the worker file is served
+   with this policy and as `.js`, because a dedicated worker obeys the policy on its own script's response, not
+   its page's (a test of a deployed map reads that response's header); and a PMTiles basemap needs `Range`
+   carried to the Conduit and `Content-Range` carried back, because without them the map loads and draws no
+   tile.

